# Git

Trunk-based. `main` is always shippable. Short-lived branches. PR into `main`. Squash merge. Do not force-push `main`.

## Branch

```
<type>/<adr-or-issue>-<short-description>
```

- `type`: `feat` `fix` `docs` `refactor` `test` `chore` `ci` `perf` `revert` `rfc`
- `adr-or-issue`: ADR number (`0001` or `adr-0001`) when implementing an accepted RFC; otherwise the GitHub issue number.
- `short-description`: lowercase kebab-case, few words.
- One ADR (or one issue) per branch. Do not pile unrelated work.

Examples: `feat/0001-session-store`, `fix/42-null-user`, `rfc/0003-rate-limits`, `chore/12-gitignore`

Trivial loop-skip (typo, one-liner, no ticket): `chore/skip-<slug>`.

Create the branch before `/implement`. Never commit RFC/ADR/plan work on `main`.

## Commit

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <description>
```

- Imperative, lowercase description, no trailing period.
- `scope` optional: area (`auth`, `rfc`, `harness`).
- **Body required:** after a blank line, bullet list of changes from the diff (what landed, not a repeat of the subject).
- Breaking change: put `!` after type or after `)`: `feat(auth)!: replace sessions with jwt`
- Footer `BREAKING CHANGE: <what>` only when `!` is used and the human needs the migration note.
- One logical change per commit. Do not mix format-only with behavior.

Examples:

```
feat(auth): persist sessions in redis

- store session tokens in redis
- drop in-memory session map
```

```
feat(auth)!: drop cookie sessions

- issue jwt access tokens
- remove session cookie middleware

BREAKING CHANGE: clients must send Authorization bearer tokens
```

## Pull request

When the user asks to open a pull request (merge request), create one. Do not open a PR unsolicited after a commit.

1. Must be on a feature branch, not `main`. Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed.
2. Title: squash Conventional Commit — `type(scope): description` (latest subject or the PR theme).
3. Body: fill [`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`](.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md). **Summary** and **Changes** come from `git log main..HEAD` (subjects + bullet bodies). Link RFC / ADR / plan paths when this branch implements one. Check **Breaking** if any commit has `!`.
4. Create with `gh pr create --title "..." --body "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"` (HEREDOC, template structure). Base `main`.
5. **The reply to the user must include the pull request URL.** If `gh` fails, print the error and the compare URL; do not pretend the PR exists.

Use `/pr` when that skill is available. Squash merge. CI green if the repo has checks.
